	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/markdown" rect="(820.0, 20.0, 400.0, 230.0)" font-family="Sans Serif" font-size="16">*Chapter 7. 7A: compare the two Sentiment Analysis methods with the Label column. 7B: Box Plot, choose compound (or sentiment) as the variable and Sentiment for Group by. 7C: Preprocess Text with Lowercase, Regexp, English stopwords and a Document frequency filter (relative 0.01 to 1.0); Bag of Words with Count. Test and Score: Naive Bayes on the words takes a couple of minutes. Corpus: the text feature is Review (7B) and Sentence (7A). Sentiment Analysis does not use Preprocess Text: VADER reads the raw text.*</text>
	</annotations>
